## 🛠 Debugging Insertion Sort

Below are buggy versions. Find the mistake and **fix it in your head like a pro**.

---

### 🧪 Buggy Code 1 – Misplaced Assignment

```c
void insertionSort1(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        int key = arr[i];
        int j = i;

        while (j > 0 && arr[j - 1] > key) {
            arr[j] = arr[j - 1];
            // ❌ missing something here
        }

        arr[j] = key;
    }
}
```

❓ What's wrong?

---

✅ **Fix:** You forgot to **decrement `j`** inside the while loop.  
Without `j--`, it becomes an infinite loop or just wrong behavior.

```c
while (j > 0 && arr[j - 1] > key) {
    arr[j] = arr[j - 1];
    j--; // ✅
}
```

