void insertionSort3(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { // ❌ bug
        int key = arr[i];
        int j = i - 1;

        while (j >= 0 && arr[j] > key) {
            arr[j + 1] = arr[j];
            j--;
        }

        arr[j + 1] = key;
    }
}
```

❓ What's wrong?

---

✅ **Fix:** First iteration (i = 0) is unnecessary — it's already “sorted”.  
Start from `i = 1`.

```c
for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) // ✅
```

